  "text": "Peter and John looked into the empty tomb and went home. She stayed. So she is the one who saw him. John twenty. Mary Magdalene comes to the tomb while it is still dark, sees the stone gone, and runs for Peter and John. They sprint back. Look in. See the linen. And then the text says it plainly. They went away again unto their own home. They left. She did not. Mary stood without at the sepulchre weeping. So she is the one still there when two angels ask her why she is crying. And she says, \"They have taken away my Lord, and I know not where they have laid him.\" Then she turns around, sees a man, and thinks he is the gardener. \"Sir, if thou have borne him hence, tell me where thou hast laid him, and I will take him away.\" She is devastated and still trying to handle the logistics herself. She is going to carry a body. And he says one word. \"Mary.\" That is it. That is the whole thing. He says her name and she knows. Then he sends her. Go to my brethren and tell them. And Mary Magdalene came and told the disciples that she had seen the Lord. The resurrection gets announced by the woman who would not leave the graveyard.",
